# Paper C: counts `(2,2,2,2)` — the flows at the kinks of the band frontier

`g = (a, a, -a, -a, b, b, -b, -b)`, `D = 4(a+b)`, `q = a² - 10ab + 17b²`, `p = a² - 14ab + 25b²`
(smaller roots `a/b = 5 - 2√2` and `7 - 2√6`). Each flow is a mixture of type sequences, every
sequence together with its sign flip, with weights `n_j / Q` polynomial in `(a, b)`; each meets
its band `E/Q` and its budget cost bound `(QW/Q)/D` at every budget (all seven budget costs are
equal to the bound). `flow_mixQ` turns the cleared inequalities into a flow. Generated by
`scratchpad/c2222f/gen_kink.py` after the exact checks of `kspec.py` (weights, every band
inequality and every budget cost, on the whole region; the weights proportional to `p` or `q`
use the sign hypotheses).

